<title>USA: First Nationwide unit wraps $500 mln share offer.</title>
<headline>First Nationwide unit wraps $500 mln share offer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A real estate investment trust created by Los Angeles-based First Nationwide Bank has completed an offering of 20 million preferred shares valued at $500 million, a Goldman, Sachs and Co executive said on Friday.</p>
<p>Known as First Nationwide Preferred Capital Corp, the REIT initially planned to sell eight million so-called perpetual preferred stock with a value of $200 million.</p>
